From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 09:00:24 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] drm/apple: test the T8132 panel EDR words and the HDR panel
 EDID

KUnit suite apple-dcp-m4-edr for dcp-m4-edr.h with the J604's ADT values
(1600 nit peak, potential headroom 16.0, 600 nit SDR maximum): the
binary64 encoding, the offsets of each word in the swap record and the
words left out, the start ramp to peak / SDR white, the headroom cap at
dim SDR white, a brightness change during EDR, the end of EDR in one
swap, the ramp after a blank, and that SDR frames carry nothing.

Two apple-dcp-panel-edid cases: the CTA-861 block of an HDR panel (BT.2020
RGB, SDR and PQ, 1600 nits as luminance code 160) in a valid three-block
EDID, and the connector reading the PQ capability back from it.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/Makefile              |   1 +
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-edr-test.c     | 198 ++++++++++++++++++++
 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-panel-edid-test.c |  76 ++++++++
 3 files changed, 275 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 drivers/gpu/drm/apple/dcp-m4-edr-test.c

